    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T10:34:48Z",
    "body": "This is the same test as #3116 (closed by a green run without a code change). The failing step is motion suites: adaptive_troch_parallel - wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes, FAIL in 106 s, flagged slow (>60 s). The only merge between the green tip 6b63e442b and this red tip 7d1f1d72c is PR #3118, which changes crates/post only - no motion, geometry or cl file. Four runner results on unchanged motion code: green 64 s, red 145 s, red 140 s, green, red 106 s. That is a load-sensitive wall-time test, not a code break.\n\nThe fix is the one planned on #3116: remove the runner-load assumption from the test (no wall-time bound in an assertion; give it a smaller fixture or move it to the heavy lane per AGENTS.md \"A test that takes more than about 60 s in debug moves to the heavy lane\"). Branch issue/3116-parallel-lane-timing holds the start of that work. The run on the current tip e3db8dfad will say whether main is green again; a green there closes this issue the same way it closed #3116.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
